  "guideContent": {
    "strategyOverview": "Sauron, the Dark Lord turns the whole table into fuel: every spell an opponent casts amasses Orcs 1, so one Army creature grows all game without you spending a card. When that Army connects, the Ring tempts you, and each temptation lets Sauron discard your hand and draw four cards. The deck leans into both halves. Amass multipliers (Mauhúr, The Great Goblin) turn every counter batch into extra bodies of damage, and a dense Ring-temptation package (Call of the Ring, Nazgûl, In the Darkness Bind Them, Soothing of Sméagol) keeps the draw-four engine firing every turn. Discarding your hand is a resource, not a cost: Reanimate, Gathering of Darkness, and Treason of Isengard buy the best cards back from the graveyard, and Windfall turns an empty post-tempt hand into a fresh seven. The deck wins through combat with one enormous evasive Army (trample, menace, deathtouch, unblockable), an Assault on Osgiliath double-strike burst, The Great Goblin converting counter batches into direct damage, or the One Ring to Rule Them All mill-and-drain. 72 of the 99 cards carry a printing from the four Tolkien sets (Tales of Middle-earth, its Commander decks, The Hobbit, and The Hobbit Eternal).",
